# Starforge — module ownership

**One engine per concern.** Every product capability has a single owning module (or Core port). New work **calls** that owner; it does not fork a second cart, form builder, media library, SMTP stack, profile store, or payment UI.

## Continuously document

When a boundary is decided or sharpened (who owns price, fulfillment, shipping, entitlements, chrome):

1. Update the owner’s **README** (Shipped / Owns / Consumes).
2. Update or add the matching **`.cursor/rules/sf-*-module.mdc`** when the concern is cross-cutting (Forms, Payments, UI).
3. Reflect it in **`docs/project-context/docs/`** (platform layers, pack plans) so agents and humans share one map.

Do not leave ownership only in chat. If it is clear in your head, it must be clear in the repo.

## Revenue spine (why Payments is foundational)

The platform’s commercial base is **modular checkout**, not a shop monolith. MVP money flows that must work end-to-end:

| Flow | Domain owner (catalog / rules / fulfillment) | Checkout / money movement |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Subscriptions** (plans, highlight, entitlements) | **`product:subscriptions`** (when shipped) | **`product:payments`** |
| **Events tickets** | **`product:events`** | **`product:payments`** |
| **Ads** (packages, credits, campaigns) | **`product:ads`** | **`product:payments`** |
| **Shop** (SKUs, shipping) | **`product:shop`** — **later** | **`product:payments`** |
| **Marketplace** fees / boosts | Owning marketplace / listings pack | **`product:payments`** (same cart/orders) |

Shop is deferred; subscriptions, event tickets, and ads are the **revenue strategy floor**. Marketplace later reuses the same payments + domain layers (e.g. highlight via subscriptions).

## Ownership test

Ask: *which module would you delete to remove this concept?* That module owns it.

| Example | Owner | Not owner |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Cart, order, VAT line, gateway, invoice series | **payments** | Events / Ads / Shop |
| Tier capacity, waitlist, ticket fulfillment | **events** | payments |
| Plan period, entitlement grant, “highlight” product | **subscriptions** | payments |
| Ad package, placement, campaign credit balance | **ads** | payments |
| Shipping rate / zone / delivery quote | **shop** | payments cart |
| Registration field schema | **forms** | events / payments |
| Receipt email copy / transport | **email-manager** (+ Core Mailer) | payments SMTP |

Payments stores **`sourceModule` + price snapshot** on lines; consumers **re-resolve** domain prices server-side at checkout and run **fulfillment hooks** on paid / expire / refund.

## Do

- Prefer extending the owning pack’s API over adding parallel tables in a consumer.
- Deep-link admin to the owner (`/admin/payments`, `/admin/forms`, …) instead of duplicating settings.
- When adding a new pack that touches money, forms, media, or identity — wire to existing owners first; document the consume edge.

## Don’t

- Put shipping math in the cart engine — shop owns delivery; payments only accepts quoted line amounts from the owner.
- Put subscription billing rules or ad auction logic inside payments.
- Rebuild Forms / Media / Email / Profiles inside any commercial pack.

